[["text","LESSON 03 / 31 • ORIGINAL CHECKLIST"],["heading","3. Linked lists (singly and doubly)"],["text","English: Nodes connected by references; doubly linked nodes also have previous references."],["sinhala","","සිංහල: Node එකක data සහ next reference තිJයනවො. Doubly list එJක් previous reference",460],["sinhala","","එකත් තිJයනවො.",87],["text","Real-world example: Playlist"],["code","10 -> 20 -> 30 -> null"],["code","10 <-> 20 <-> 30"],["heading","Java example / illustration"],["code","LinkedList<Integer> a = new LinkedList<>();\na.add(10); a.add(20); a.addFirst(5);\nSystem.out.println(a); // [5, 10, 20]"],["heading","Complexity and trade-offs"],["text","Index/search O(n); known-node insertion O(1)."],["heading","Interview question"],["heading","Array vs linked list?"],["text","Arrays offer direct index access; linked lists allow local pointer updates."],["heading","Quick practice"],["text","Explain this concept aloud, trace the example, and describe when you would choose this"],["text","structure over an alternative."]]